desc.intro:
One chat (Chats → chat → ⋮ “More options” → “Chat as JSON”): the messages of a chosen period or of one topic — who wrote when, replies, corrections, attachments (name and size), reactions, pins — plus the topics and the tasks and appointments that came out of the chat. For the archive and for an assistant to read, summarise or sort.

What the import does (always in the chat open in the app; first a list of changes with warnings, saved only after “Import”):
- Topics without "id" — creates new ones (a topic with the same name that already exists is used). Topics with "id" — renames ("title") or closes and opens ("closed"); allowed for whoever created the topic or a leader.
- Messages with "id" (from the export) — only sorting: moving to another topic ("topic"; the message's author or a leader), pinning ("pinned"; leaders) and saving for yourself ("starred").
- Messages without "id" — NEW messages of the person importing: with their first and last name (as when writing by hand), with the moment of sending and the mark “From an import”, which everyone sees; or scheduled for later ("sendAt"). At most {maxPosts} in one import; their message with the same content that is already in the chat (or already waiting, scheduled) doesn't go a second time.
- Message content and topic names are encrypted in the browser with the chat key — just like those written by hand. The export file contains them in plain text: it is your copy.

What the import never does — and why. A message is someone's statement, signed with the key of its author's role. The import can only add your new words (visibly marked) and tidy the chat:
- it doesn't write in someone else's name — a new message with another person's "author" is skipped;
- it doesn't write backwards — "at" says when a message was written; a new message with "at" is skipped (instead "sendAt": sending in the future);
- it doesn't change the content, sender or time of existing messages — yours included (you correct them in the chat: “Edit”, with edit history);
- it doesn't delete messages or topics — what is not in the document stays as it is;
- it doesn't move messages from another chat and doesn't paste them here as new;
- it doesn't add files (the JSON only has their names), reactions, tasks or appointments;
- it doesn't take a quote from the document — a reply's quote comes from the real message ("replyTo").
Whoever only reads in the chat has the export alone. The export covers at most {maxExport} messages.
Return ONE JSON object, without comments.
